From b7f176b582e6b0dcf911c72125e1825ac479b057 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds bootstrap <bootstrap@invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:14:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hardware addresses: use the port's memory and register macros
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)

The game code still dereferenced DS addresses by literal in 20 places -- some
written with the leading zero dropped (0x6010000, 0x6400000), which is how the
first sweep missed three of them. The port's memory areas are ordinary arrays
(patch 1301), so a literal such as 0x04000000 or 0x027E0000 points at unmapped
memory on the 3DS and on host32.

Two crashes in normal play, both from this class:

- The tall-grass wild encounter aborted on its first battle frame (log-10):
  WirelessStatusIcon_LoadChar reads DISPCNT through 0x04000000 to pick the OBJ
  character mapping, right after the battle overlays load. Trainer and link
  battles take the same Battle_CreateWirelessStatusIcon path.
- With that fixed, the battle got as far as its background and aborted in
  BattleSystem_SetBackground (log-11): MIi_CpuCopy32 copies 0x10000 bytes from
  BG VRAM 0x06010000, and the terrain pass then reads OBJ VRAM 0x06400000.

The same class, converted here:

- I/O registers: DISPCNT / DB_DISPCNT in the wireless status icon and the spin
  trade app, and the G3 swap-buffers request in the Pokemon summary, now use
  reg_GX_DISPCNT, reg_GXS_DB_DISPCNT and reg_G3_SWAP_BUFFERS (all built on
  HW_REG_BASE, which 1301 points at NitroPort_IoReg).
- The battle background uses HW_BG_VRAM + 0x10000 and HW_OBJ_VRAM.
- Nine DTCM IRQ-check writes (eight V-blank handlers and the trade animation
  task) use HW_DTCM -- already the port's DTCM array, and on the DS the same
  linker symbol -- instead of 0x027E0000; the code after them is unchanged.
- The encounter effect's clear of the display-capture VRAM uses
  HW_LCDC_VRAM + 0x40000. The comment said bank D; 0x06840000 is bank C in the
  LCDC view (A at 0x06800000, then one 128 KB bank every 0x20000), and the
  reg_GX_DISPCAPCNT = 0xC0320C04 destination is bank C too. Display capture is
  not implemented in the port yet, so the effect still will not show the
  captured field, but it no longer faults.
- The wireless seed (0x027FFC3C) and the reboot-into-file flag (0x027FFC2C)
  use HW_MAIN_MEM + the same offset.

Every change is inside #ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS with the original lines kept in the
#else, so the DS text preprocesses unchanged. system_card.c's ROM-header
mirrors were already handled this way; the reboot flag was missed.

not converted, with reason: sub/lib/src/sound_driver.c's REG_POWCNT2
(0x04000304) is only used by SND_BeginSleep/EndSleep, whose caller,
power_manager_driver.c, is not built for the port; the wireless sub/ sources
(wl_*, wmsp_*, wvr_*) are the ARM7 Wi-Fi stack, which the port stubs.

Checked: tests/test_hw_addresses.py (new) preprocesses the game sources for the
port and reports every one of these, including the 7-digit forms, while
ignoring the DS-only #else copies; the fixed tree reports none. The 3DS ELF's
LoadChar now loads NitroPort_IoReg (0x00d889e0) from the literal pool instead
of moving 0x04000000, and BattleSystem_SetBackground uses the port's VRAM
arrays. The end-to-end battle is the owner's hardware run.
